    "reply": "The retrieved records cover the associated conditions and a set of ClinVar missense variants in the NM_007294.4 transcript, but not the gene record, genetic tests, or literature. One of the associated conditions is Hereditary breast ovarian cancer syndrome [2]. The variants include NM_007294.4(BRCA1):c.4709T>C (p.Leu1570Pro) [1].\n\n## Associated Conditions\n\nHereditary breast ovarian cancer syndrome is one of the retrieved conditions [2]. Hereditary cancer-predisposing syndrome is also among them [4]. Familial breast-ovarian cancer susceptibility 1 is a third [12].\n\n## ClinVar Missense Variants\n\nThe variant records are single-nucleotide substitutions on NM_007294.4 that each predict an amino-acid change. In the N-terminal region, one example is NM_007294.4(BRCA1):c.353T>C (p.Leu118Pro) [5]. Another is NM_007294.4(BRCA1):c.500C>T (p.Thr167Ile) [24]. The central region is represented by NM_007294.4(BRCA1):c.3664G>A (p.Glu1222Lys) [3].\n\n## Record Identifiers\n\nThe variant NM_007294.4(BRCA1):c.4709T>C (p.Leu1570Pro) is ClinVar:1000183 [1]. NM_007294.4(BRCA1):c.4685C>G (p.Pro1562Arg) is ClinVar:1005528 [15]. NM_007294.4(BRCA1):c.1328A>G (p.Lys443Arg) is ClinVar:1010509 [30]. The records do not state a clinical significance for any of these variants, and the retrieved set did not include the gene record, genetic test listings, or key literature.",
